  "action": "In general, a standard system update will make all the necessary changes.",
  "cves": [
    "CVE-2026-13204"
  ],
  "description": "It was discovered that Bind incorrectly handled DNSSEC validation when a\ndomain was covered by both NSEC and NSEC3 records with only one type having\nan RRSIG. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to cause Bind to\ncrash, resulting in a denial of service.",
  "id": "USN-8696-1",
  "isummary": "Bind could be made to crash if it received specially crafted network\ntraffic.",
